00:06:16,666 --> 00:06:22,666
If you can't get out, get even.

2
00:12:33,333 --> 00:12:39,333
The Longest Yard is a drama, comedy, crime film directed by Peter Segal.

3
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:56,000
Disgraced pro football quarterback Paul Crewe lands in a Texas federal penitentiary, where manipulative
Warden Hazen recruits him to advise the institution's football team of prison guards.

4
00:25:06,666 --> 00:25:12,666
Crewe suggests a tune-up game which lands him quarterbacking a
crew of inmates in a game against the guards.

5
00:31:23,333 --> 00:31:29,333
Aided by incarcerated ex-NFL coach and player Nate Scarborough, Crewe and his team must overcome not only the
bloodthirstiness of the opposition, but also the corrupt warden trying to fix the game against them.

6
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:46,000
Paul Crewe, played by Adam Sandler.

7
00:43:56,666 --> 00:44:02,666
Caretaker, played by Chris Rock.

8
00:50:13,333 --> 00:50:19,333
Warden Hazen, played by James Cromwell.

9
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:36,000
Coach Nate Scarborough, played by Burt Reynolds.

10
01:02:46,666 --> 01:02:52,666
Megget, played by Nelly.

11
01:09:03,333 --> 01:09:09,333
Cheeseburger Eddy, played by Terry Crews.

12
01:15:20,000 --> 01:15:26,000
The Longest Yard is a 2005 American sports comedy film directed
by Peter Segal and written by Sheldon Turner.

13
01:21:36,666 --> 01:21:42,666
A remake of 1974's film of the same name, it stars Adam Sandler as a washed-up former professional American
football quarterback who goes to prison and is forced to assemble a team to play against the guards.

14
01:27:53,333 --> 01:27:59,333
The film co-stars Chris Rock, James Cromwell, Nelly, William Fichtner, David Patrick Kelly, Tracy
Morgan, Cloris Leachman, and Burt Reynolds, who played Sandler's role in the original.

15
01:34:10,000 --> 01:34:16,000
It was released by Paramount Pictures in the United States and Canada, and Sony Pictures Releasing–under the Columbia Pictures label–in other territories on
May 27, 2005, to negative reviews from critics, but the film was a box office success by grossing $191.2 million on an $82 million budget.

16
01:40:26,666 --> 01:40:32,666
The film explores themes of prison, corruption,
prisoner, smuggling (contraband), sports.

17
01:46:43,333 --> 01:46:49,333
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
